From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:40:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rasterize recorded scenes in bounded row bands

A caller renders a recorded scene band by band, without allocating its full pixel buffer, by
passing a negative y offset (upstream's signed `RasterizerSettings::offset`). PreparedRender
prepares glyph resources once and keeps them with the recorded context until every band is
rendered, so a band cannot evict glyphs a later band needs. A band whose offset is negative is
still fully covered by the scene, so it skips the explicit clear.
